      "rationale": "Torch already ran and satisfies required observations: collective identity, logical payload and cross-rank matching show one flush of 13 SUM allreduces (12x 28,351,488B + 1x 157,541,376B, f32, world 2, RING_LL on stream 17) with bucket identity resolved by observed gradient-storage membership, so no collector is re-requested for identity. The objective gap is rank asymmetry: rank 0 kernel sum is 285.8ms vs 63.6ms on rank 1; within a single rank clock, rank 0's 13 kernels are back-to-back (sub-2us gaps, first kernel 101ms) while rank 1's 27MB kernels last ~3.5ms with ~11ms compute-filled gaps, indicating rank 0's kernel time is mostly spin-wait for the later-arriving rank, not wire time. Selected collectors target exactly that: collective_calibration runs a separate synthetic full-world SUM allreduce at the observed sizes/dtypes as a reference for isolated wire cost of 28,351,488B and 157,541,376B (not a lower bound or critical-path estimate); execution_timeline provides CPU-to-CUDA submit associations, matched-submission cross-rank skew bounds, per-device intervals and passive post-accumulate gradient bucket membership to quantify arrival skew and rank-0 compute/NCCL overlap; nsys (available) resolves on-device overlap and stream contiguity questions across both ranks, while acknowledging it cannot by itself separate NCCL wait from transfer or prove bucket identity (identity already observed); device_telemetry's device-wide NVML PCIe rates and utilization during the comm phase corroborate whether the interconnect is saturated (peer access is disabled in both directions, so transport capacity is a live question) without claiming per-collective bytes. python_runtime is excluded: there is no host-dispatch evidence gap (coverage shows 0 unassociated kernels and a regular per-bucket cadence) and cProfile perturbs execution without giving GPU compute durations. candidate_diagnostics is excluded because no candidate transformation exists yet, and execution_timeline never drives subsequent search actions."
